======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  Depth-matched curl templates (six depths), galaxy fixed effects and a kernel-shape slope, on 1214 deep-MOND SPARC
  points from 88 discs.  THE STRUCTURE OF THE RESULT: the curl template and the stellar mass-to-light ratio are
  degenerate on SPARC -- both are monotonic radial shapes -- so A depends on the assumed M/L.  With M/L FREE the fit
  prefers A ~ 1, but only by shifting the mass-to-light ratio by ~0.6 dex (Upsilon 0.5 -> ~2), which population
  synthesis excludes.  Every such solution is disqualified by its own shuffle-null floor as well.
